# Code Comments

- Keep production code comments concise and focused on domain intent or non-obvious behavior.
- Do not add comments describing the AI's reasoning, implementation decisions, or thought process.
- Do not explain obvious code or describe code line-by-line.
- Do not add long comments to justify a simple implementation.
- Prefer self-explanatory code, meaningful names, and proper abstractions over comments.
- Only add a comment when it provides information that cannot reasonably be inferred from the code itself.
- Avoid speculative comments about why existing code or the original implementation behaves a certain way.
- When modifying existing code, preserve the existing comment style and avoid introducing unnecessary comments.